hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24280","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Umar narrated to us, from Umayyah ibn Safwan, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Zuhayr, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in his sermon at al-Nabawwah, or al-Banawwah, of al-Ta'if: Soon you will know the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire, or: Your best from your worst, and I know it only as he said: The people of Paradise from the people of the Fire. So a speaker from among the Muslims said: By what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: By good praise and bad praise; you are witnesses of one another."
